{"orgCode":"1045","name":"Cannabis Control Appeals Panel","agencyCode":"1000","agencyName":"Business and Consumer Services","description":"The Cannabis Control Appeals Panel (Panel) was established by Proposition 64, (the Adult Use of Marijuana Act) in November 2016 and later amended by Senate Bill 94 (Chapter 27, Statutes of 2017), which created the Medicinal and Adult-Use Cannabis Regulation and Safety Act. The Panel consists of five members—one appointed by the Senate Committee on Rules, one appointed by the Speaker of the Assembly, and three appointed by the Governor and confirmed by the Senate.\n\nThe Panel serves as an impartial appellate body for annual licensees and applicants seeking review of licensing decisions made by the Department of Cannabis Control (DCC). Through its streamlined appeals process, the Panel ensures fairness, transparency, subject-matter expertise, and due process in the review of DCC enforcement actions.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":2872,"cy":3318,"by":3443},"positions":{"py":9.5,"cy":13,"by":12},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":52,"cy":55,"by":57}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/1000/1045","kind":"department","name":"Cannabis Control Appeals Panel","code":"1045","amounts":{"py":2872,"cy":3318,"by":3443},"positions":{"py":9.5,"cy":13,"by":12},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":2872,"cy":3318,"by":3443}},"children":[{"id":"exp/1000/1045/1045","kind":"program","name":"Cannabis Appeals Panel","code":"1045","amounts":{"py":2872,"cy":3318,"by":3443},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":2872,"cy":3318,"by":3443}},"positions":{"py":9.5,"cy":13,"by":12},"description":"1045 - CANNABIS APPEALS PANEL\n\nThe Cannabis Control Appeals Panel provides quasi-judicial administrative review of licensing decisions issued by the Department of Cannabis Control.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2924,"cy":3373,"by":3500}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/1000/1045/1045/f3288","kind":"fund","name":"Cannabis Control Fund","code":"3288","amounts